    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22322": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Part-Time Academic (STAT 4620.03/5620.03: Data Analysis) - Winter 2027 Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Part-Time Academic (STAT 4620.03/5620.03: Data Analysis) - Winter 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Academic (STAT 4620.03/5620.03: Data Analysis) - Winter 2027 Posting Number PTAP3555P Department/Unit Mathematics & Statistics Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Job Summary & Key Responsibilities The Part-Time Academic will teach the half-credit course, STAT 4620.03/5620.03: Data Analysis, during the Winter Term (January – April 2027). The course is scheduled TR from 1305–1425. Responsibilities include course preparation, lectures, grading, and student feedback. The successful candidate will maintain 3 hours of scheduled student hours each week. Course Description : A variety of statistical models which are useful for the analysis of real data are discussed. Topics include: generalized linear models, such as logistic regression and Poisson regression, models for multidimensional contingency tables, ordered categories and survival data. Qualifications/Requirements of Position A PhD in Statistics is required. The successful applicant must have demonstrated knowledge of the subject matter. Previous teaching experience is an asset. Please provide teaching evaluations if available. Salary Range/Pay Rate Per CUPE Collective Agreement Additional Information All offers of employment as a Part-Time Academic are conditional upon sufficient student enrolment in the course and approval by the University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given 