    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22361": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Part-Time Academic (MGMT 5523: Project Management) - Winter 2027 Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Part-Time Academic (MGMT 5523: Project Management) - Winter 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Academic (MGMT 5523: Project Management) - Winter 2027 Posting Number PTAP3567P Department/Unit Faculty of Management - General Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Job Summary & Key Responsibilities A Part-Time Academic is needed to teach the following course from January 11th to April 13th, 2027. Class is currently scheduled for 11:30am to 2.30 pm on Tuesdays. This course is offered in person. This course is delivered to our full-time Master of Management (MM) students. This course examines the principles, methodologies, and practices of project management in contemporary organizations. Students develop skills in project planning, scheduling, budgeting, resource allocation, risk management, performance measurement, and stakeholder engagement. Through a semester-long project management simulation, students apply project management tools and frameworks to a realistic organizational project while responding to evolving project challenges and executive oversight. Emphasis is placed on data-driven decision-making, leadership, teamwork, and the successful delivery of projects in complex and dynamic environments. The Part-Time academic will be responsible for all aspects of teaching and administering the class, including lectures, test preparation and evaluation. The part-time academic should be available for a three-hour lecture and two hours per week for consultation with students. The part-time academic reports to Dr. Paulette Skerrett, the MM Program Director. Qualifications/Requirements of Position A graduate degree in a management related topic is required. The successful applicant must have demonstrated knowledge of the subject matter, practical experience, and record of effective teaching experience. Excellent oral/written and presentation skills are required. Considering the nature of this course, professional work experience in industry is strongly considered an asset. Salary Range/Pay Rate $8,260 per course (In accordance with CUPE Collective Agreement) Additional Information All offers of employment as a Part-Time Academic are conditional upon sufficient student enrolment in the course and approval by the University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Term of appointment January - April 2027 Open Date 10/16/2026 Close Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22338 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Teaching Statement Teaching Dossier Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22335": {
      "title": "Limited Term Assistant Professor, School of Planning",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Limited Term Assistant Professor, School of Planning Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Limited Term Assistant Professor, School of Planning Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Limited Term Assistant Professor, School of Planning Posting Number F820P Type of position Limited Term Department/Unit Planning Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada About the opportunity The School of Planning at Dalhousie University invites applications for a 2-year limited-term teaching appointment at the Assistant Professor rank, expected to start July 2027 or as negotiated. Dalhousie University, located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, is one of Canada’s top research and teaching universities. Halifax is a growing and thriving mid-sized city that occupies a distinct natural setting on the Atlantic coast, and is the academic, cultural, and economic centre of Atlantic Canada. The School of Planning at Dalhousie University serves the Atlantic region of Canada as the only professional planning school east of Quebec. The School offers graduate and undergraduate professionally accredited planning degrees (Bachelor of Planning [BPlan] and Master of Planning [MPlan]), and a research-based graduate degree (Master of Planning Studies [ MPS ]). Current enrollment stands at over 50 graduate and 150 undergraduate students. We are a leading interdisciplinary planning school, equipping the next generation of planners to create inclusive communities through experiential learning, innovative research, and partnerships. We foster and inspire planning for resilient, equitable and smart communities. Together, we embrace the core values of collaboration, innovation, diversity and inclusion. The School is looking for an outstanding candidate with proven teaching expertise in urban and regional planning. The successful candidate will be expected to teach up to four courses per academic year, supervise students, and contribute academic service in support of the School. They would be expected to be on site and deliver teaching on site in person. For more information about the School of Planning, Dalhousie University, and Halifax, please go to these websites: https://www.dal.ca/faculty/architecture-planning/school-of-planning.html https://www.dal.ca/ https://www.halifax.ca/ The preferred candidate will be able to address the School’s teaching needs in the areas of: (1) Introduction to Planning, (2) land use policy and housing studies, and (3) plan making and the planning process as well as planning studio or site planning. In addition, the candidate may be expected to coordinate the BPlan internship or MPlan work term and supervise undergraduate thesis and graduate Independent Research Project ( IRP ) students. The candidate must hold at least one recognized, accredited planning degree endorsed by the Professional Standards Board ( PSB ), as well as a relevant master’s degree. MCIP and RPP or LPP designations would be considered significant assets. In keeping with the School’s present strengths and directions, we expect the person in this position to be comfortable in an interdisciplinary setting, demonstrate leadership on collaborative activities, and bring innovative ideas to advance planning practice or research and teaching. Candidates should provide a cover letter (in PDF format) explaining which of their academic credentials is an accredited planning degree, their teaching interests, examples of course outlines, evidence of teaching effectiveness, a curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three references (who may be contacted later with the applicant’s knowledge). Queries regarding the position should be directed towards Dr. Jeffrey Biggar, Acting Director, School of Planning: dirplan@dal.ca Applications will be accepted until November 30th and must be submitted through PeopleAdmin: https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22294 . This position is a part of the Dalhousie Faculty Association ( DFA ) Bargaining Unit. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/14/2026 Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22294 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Teaching Statement Teaching Dossier List of referees Optional Documents Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
  },
